---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Experience | Norman Rasmussen" description="Professional and academic experience in software engineering, analytics, applied mathematics, and research.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Portfolio / Experience</p>
      <h1>Experience grounded in useful work.</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">Software development in an industry setting, mathematical research, and a strong foundation in computational mathematics.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="page-content">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Professional experience</p>
      <div class="timeline">
        <article class="timeline-entry">
          <span class="date">SUMMER 2026 / ATLANTA, GEORGIA</span>
          <h2>Software & analytics development — UPS</h2>
          <p>Developed Python-based data applications supporting pricing and network monitoring workflows during an internship with UPS Supply Chain Solutions / Mail Innovations.</p>
          <p>Worked with Streamlit, SQL, and data analysis tools to help users inspect trends, monitor operational data, and make informed business decisions.</p>
          <div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">Python</span><span class="tag">Streamlit</span><span class="tag">SQL</span><span class="tag">Data applications</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="timeline-entry">
          <span class="date">ACADEMIC RESEARCH / BRIGHAM YOUNG UNIVERSITY</span>
          <h2>Applied mathematics research</h2>
          <p>Contributed to computational investigations involving dynamical systems, parameter estimation, and mathematical modeling. Separate research efforts address scheduling, uncertainty, and optimization.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/research/">See research areas ↗</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="two-column" style="margin-top: 38px;">
        <div class="info-panel">
          <p class="section-label">Education</p>
          <h2>Brigham Young University</h2>
          <p>B.S. in Applied and Computational Mathematics (ACME)</p>
          <p><strong>Expected graduation:</strong> April 2027</p>
          <p>Interests include probability, stochastic processes, optimization, network theory, and mathematical foundations of machine learning.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-panel">
          <p class="section-label">Technical toolkit</p>
          <h2>Methods and technologies</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Python, SQL, C++, JavaScript, TypeScript</li>
            <li>NumPy, Pandas, SciPy, scikit-learn, PyTorch</li>
            <li>Linear/integer programming and numerical optimization</li>
            <li>Streamlit, React, Git, GitHub Actions</li>
            <li>Scientific simulation and reproducible experimentation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="notice" style="margin-top: 34px;">Professional projects are described at a high level. Proprietary employer code, client information, and internal business materials are not published on this site.</div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
